# Settings has an AI section — ghost text, its backend, the Claude and
# Codex backends, the meter, the sessions side by side, the session
# notifications and their bell (at End the first two rows, Ghost text and
# its backend, are just above the box — the Integrations section's API row
# took the second) —
# below Editor; End scrolls the box there, and the filter keeps the
# section's header over the rows it matched.
write a.txt alpha
open a.txt
command view.settings
expect screen contains "── UI ──"
expect screen contains "▸ Line numbers:"
key end
expect screen contains "Sessions side by side:"
expect screen contains "Claude backend:"
expect screen contains "[unset]"
expect screen contains "Session notifications:"
expect screen contains "off / [unfocused] / always"
expect screen contains "Session bell:"
expect screen contains "▸ Reset all to defaults"
key /
type notif
expect screen contains "── AI ──"
expect screen contains "Session notifications:"
expect screen lacks "── Editor ──"
key esc
key esc
expect screen lacks "── AI ──"
expect screen lacks "Session notifications:"
